Depends: libc6 (>= 2.28), libstdc++6 (>= 11), libgtk-3-0 (>= 3.24), dbus, libx11-6, libxext6, libxrender1, libxcomposite1, libxcursor1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxi6, libxrandr2, libxss1, libxtst6, libnss3, libasound2t64 (>= 1.2.4) | libasound2 (>= 1.2.4), libgbm1, libdrm2, mesa-vulkan-drivers | amdgpu-dkms | nvidia-driver
Homepage: https://github.com/Can-5/foxai-browser
Description: FoxAI Browser - Privacy-focused Firefox fork with offline AI
 FoxAI Browser is a privacy-hardened Firefox fork with built-in offline AI support.
 Features:
 - LibreWolf-level fingerprinting resistance (RFP + letterboxing + canvas/webgl/audio noise)
 - Offline AI mode: local LLM (qwen2.5-3b) via koboldcpp on localhost:5001
 - Tor integration, hardened prefs, no telemetry/pocket/studies
 - Portable AppImage - runs on any glibc 2.28+ distro (Fedora, Ubuntu, Debian, Arch, etc.)
 .
 This package contains the AppImage binary installed to /usr/bin/foxai-browser
 with desktop entry and icon integration.
